{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/833674-talk-to-me-of-sorcebooks","id":833674,"title":"Talk to me of Sorcebooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-19T20:04:52-08:00","id":833674,"title":"Talk to me of Sorcebooks","content":"So, I've finally gotten round to buying Demon, and am enjoying reading my fresh-smelling POD-Book right now, and the first question that come to mind after thinking &quot;Hey, this stuff is really good&quot; was &quot;So, I wonder what are the sorcebooks like?&quot;<br /> <br /> So tell me, dear friends, how are the sorcebooks and supplimentry materials? Anything good? Anything bad? Or even anything ugly? Anything you think is a must-have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T20:09:26-08:00","id":833677,"title":"","content":"The player's guide and the storyteller's guide are the only must-haves I'd say at the moment. Interface is cool reading and Heirs to Hell (Demonic Children) is interesting, but neither are particularly important. Seattle and the Seed Collection are interesting plot hooks, but again I wouldn't call them necessary either. Definitely full of ideas though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:08:22-08:00","id":833697,"title":"","content":"The <b>Demon Player's Guide</b> and <b>Demon Storyteller's Guide</b> are at about an equal level of quality at what they respectively do, and are the best bang for your buck to expand your Demon game. The <b>DPG</b> took a perspective on the demonic mind in demonic form and the impact of perfect recall I wasn't quite on board with, and I felt its section on hacking infrastructure was lackluster in delivering on the breadth of possibility the idea implies, but there's some good thought otherwise into the demonic condition, facades are extremely useful for a game, and if you liked the Embeds, Exploits and demonic forms in the corebook, the DPG will deliver more in a similar vein. The <b>DSG</b> has a pretty strong grip on the setting, provides further advice on preparing the Cipher, expands on what you can do with angels, exiles and further manifestations of the God-Machine, and has three excellent alternate setting layouts, plus a bevvy of miscellaneous hooks.<br /> <br /> <b>Splintered City: Seattle</b>'s really good. I'm not normally a fan of the city sourcebooks, but while not without its flaws, Seattle has some really strong, punchy, concise material in there, including a lot of stuff that isn't too unique to Seattle to be unable to export to other settings.<br /> <br /> <b>Heirs to Hell</b> is a book you already know whether you want or not. If you want it, get it, it's pretty solid. If you don't want it, you don't need it. There are some kinks (I don't like what the Demon-Blooded Cipher implies about the setting personally, and there's some odd framing involving Mendelian genetics), but the fluff is solid and contains one of the best lines in the game, and the fluff and mechanics together equip you to do a lot thematically with demon-blooded. If you didn't already have interest in the demon-blooded, though, I don't think it's a book that will turn you around on that, and since it keeps that focus clear, it's not got much outside the demon-blooded.<br /> <br /> The <b>Demon Translation Guide</b> is hiding a secret: it's actually got a supply of mechanical widgets to expand your game of Descent even if you know nothing about Demon: The Fallen. If you do have access to DtF, it has a chapter of evocative hooks on how two very different choirs of fallen angel might meet and complicate one another's lives, but even if you don't, Eric Zawadski tightly packed a lot of demonic form powers converted from DtF, most of which don't require you to reference the DtF book. It also has House Conditions that function like Agenda Conditions \u2013 and that therefore make good substitutes if you have a character for whom the standard Agenda Conditions don't well fit. It's less material than the other books, for sure, but it's also less price. It's a good deal if you have players who enjoy the custom-build aspect of Descent.<br /> <br /> The <b>Demon Interface</b> and the <b>Demon Seed Collection</b> haven't made a big impact on me. Certainly not ugly, just okay.<br /> <br /> DtD doesn't have a &quot;must buy&quot; the way Tome of the Mysteries is a must for first edition Mage: the Awakening, but in terms of the one book that opens up the game the most, I'd go with the <b>Storyteller's Guide.</b> It helps underline the breadth of what demons can end up facing in a Descent game, both in terms of widening what &quot;just another angel&quot; can really be, and supplementing that with odder phenomena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:15:40-08:00","id":833699,"title":"","content":"The Players Guide and and Story Tellers Guide are essential.<br /> <br /> Heirs to Hell is well written small supplement I strongly recommend. The normalcy of driving the kids to school and cooking dinner throws the G-M and its horrors into stark relief, and balancing the demands of the Descent and raising a family is a strong source of dramatic tension. Having human relationships and emotional vulnerabilities gives the Unchained a human dimension that's missing when they're just full time supernatural spies who go around fighting angels. <br /> <br /> The other stuff is useful, but you can live without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T05:35:45-08:00","id":833787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/833674-talk-to-me-of-sorcebooks?p=833697#post833697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The <b>Demon Translation Guide</b> iEric Zawadski tightly packed a lot of demonic form powers converted from DtF, most of which don't require you to reference the DtF book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I had the book, but had not read it yet, and did not know this. Took a look now and they are great! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}